  "id": "thalamotomy",
  "term": "thalamotomy",
  "definition": "Thalamotomy is a surgery that targets the thalamus to reduce major symptoms such as tremor, other unwanted movements, seizures, and related poor quality of life. Its benefits are understood as coming partly from changes in brain activity and connectivity.",
